DECISIONS 365, CONFORMANCE.md §2.3: the cpp types emit opens Dst, so the method strong, which reads self.dst, is E8019 `OpenEnumFn`; weight, which reads only self.amount of the same record, is unaffected.
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// A destination.
enum Dst { str, sta }

/// A bonus.
record Bonus {
  /// Where.
  dst: Dst
  /// How much.
  amount: Int

  /// Whether it adds strength past k.
  export fn strong(k: Int) -> Bool { return dst == Dst.str and amount > k }

  /// Its weight, k times.
  export fn weight(k: Int) -> Int { return amount * k }
}

test "strong and weight" {
  let b = Bonus { dst: Dst.str, amount: 2 }
  expect b.strong(1)
  expect b.weight(2) == 4
}

emit cpp { out: "@features/a/cpp", namespace: "a", mode: types, open: [Dst] }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8019]  a/a.canon:15:13
  emit cpp in types mode cannot generate a translated function that takes or reads an enum its package's emit of this target opens; decide on the member's Known check in your own code, or take the enum out of open

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
